1
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:07,660
[Intro — close vocal, filtered pulse]

2
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:16,197
You still there?

3
00:00:16,197 --> 00:00:24,495
Leave it on.

4
00:00:24,495 --> 00:00:24,495
[Verse 1 — restrained, dry drums enter]

5
00:00:24,495 --> 00:00:28,803
I found your name at half past two,

6
00:00:28,803 --> 00:00:31,277
with half a world between our rooms.

7
00:00:31,277 --> 00:00:37,420
We'd spent our days inside a feed

8
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:41,170
that had a price for everything.

9
00:00:41,170 --> 00:00:45,399
You showed me where the river bends,

10
00:00:45,399 --> 00:00:49,707
the timber stacked beside the wall.

11
00:00:49,707 --> 00:00:53,936
There wasn't much to look at yet.

12
00:00:53,936 --> 00:00:59,362
We stayed until the lamps came on.

13
00:00:59,362 --> 00:00:59,362
[Pre-Chorus — bass opens, voice remains close]

14
00:00:59,362 --> 00:01:01,516
You left a gap beside the gate.

15
00:01:01,516 --> 00:01:03,750
I asked what you were saving for.

16
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:05,824
You said, "We haven't met them yet,"

17
00:01:05,824 --> 00:01:09,335
and went on working in the rain.

18
00:01:09,335 --> 00:01:09,335
[Chorus — wide melody, hard drums, no shouting]

19
00:01:09,335 --> 00:01:11,410
Let them sell another future.

20
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:17,793
We're still working on this one.

21
00:01:17,793 --> 00:01:19,947
There's a light across the water

22
00:01:19,947 --> 00:01:24,734
and a door we haven't hung.

23
00:01:24,734 --> 00:01:28,484
Something that stays

24
00:01:28,484 --> 00:01:30,239
when the feed moves on.

25
00:01:30,239 --> 00:01:30,798
Something that stays

26
00:01:30,798 --> 00:01:31,755
when the feed moves on.

27
00:01:31,755 --> 00:01:32,394
Something that stays

28
00:01:32,394 --> 00:01:33,750
when the feed moves on.

29
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:37,101
Something that stays

30
00:01:37,101 --> 00:01:43,005
when the feed moves on.

31
00:01:43,005 --> 00:01:43,005
[Verse 2 — darker bass, distant metallic resonance]

32
00:01:43,005 --> 00:01:46,436
Warpkeep—Hyperion dreamed in stone,

33
00:01:46,436 --> 00:01:50,665
the starways grown through root and rain.

34
00:01:50,665 --> 00:01:54,176
A river threads a thousand doors;

35
00:01:54,176 --> 00:01:57,686
the old tombs let tomorrow in.

36
00:01:57,686 --> 00:01:59,202
The Core keeps dreaming underneath,

37
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:07,500
where no one hears the turning gears.

38
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:11,809
Above it, someone lights the forge.

39
00:02:11,809 --> 00:02:16,277
Above it, someone's waiting here.

40
00:02:16,277 --> 00:02:16,277
[Pre-Chorus — tension rises without getting louder]

41
00:02:16,277 --> 00:02:18,431
An empire is a distant thing.

42
00:02:18,431 --> 00:02:20,585
The work is close enough to touch.

43
00:02:20,585 --> 00:02:22,660
You put another beam in place.

44
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:26,090
For once, that feels like enough.

45
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:26,090
[Chorus — fuller harmony]

46
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:28,245
Let them sell another future.

47
00:02:28,245 --> 00:02:34,707
We're still working on this one.

48
00:02:34,707 --> 00:02:36,782
There's a light across the water

49
00:02:36,782 --> 00:02:41,569
and a door we haven't hung.

50
00:02:41,569 --> 00:02:45,319
Something that stays

51
00:02:45,319 --> 00:02:50,106
when the feed moves on.

52
00:02:50,106 --> 00:02:53,777
Something that stays

53
00:02:53,777 --> 00:02:55,452
when the feed moves on.

54
00:02:55,452 --> 00:02:55,452
[Bridge — stripped beat, almost conversational singing]

55
00:02:55,452 --> 00:02:56,649
On Farcaster, I bought your song.

56
00:02:56,649 --> 00:03:03,830
You said it kept the lights on.

57
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,745
A hundred little trades like that—

58
00:03:05,745 --> 00:03:07,899
a street where nothing stood before.

59
00:03:07,899 --> 00:03:10,053
Let companies keep their signs.

60
00:03:10,053 --> 00:03:12,367
We'll keep the names we answer to.

61
00:03:12,367 --> 00:03:14,282
I don't need to own your world.

62
00:03:14,282 --> 00:03:24,282
I need a way to get to you.

63
00:03:34,149 --> 00:03:34,149
[Instrumental break — distorted bass and the opening motif]

64
00:03:34,149 --> 00:03:34,149
[Final Chorus — emotionally open, layered harmonies]

65
00:03:34,149 --> 00:03:36,223
Let them sell another future.

66
00:03:36,223 --> 00:03:42,686
We're still working on this one.

67
00:03:42,686 --> 00:03:44,840
There's a light across the water

68
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:49,628
and a door we've finally hung.

69
00:03:49,628 --> 00:03:53,378
Something that stays

70
00:03:53,378 --> 00:03:58,165
when the feed moves on.

71
00:03:58,165 --> 00:03:59,362
Something that stays.

72
00:03:59,362 --> 00:04:06,622
I'm still here.

73
00:04:06,622 --> 00:04:14,840
Leave it on.

74
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:14,840
[Outro — drums fall away, unfinished synth resonance]

75
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:19,069
The river runs.

76
00:04:19,069 --> 00:04:23,537
The window glows.

77
00:04:23,537 --> 00:04:27,766
You still there?

78
00:04:27,766 --> 00:04:32,963
I'm still here.

